- Capture real outcomes and user corrections. Morrow may propose a reusable skill from repeated work, but must show it for review before saving/activating it.
- Run candidate skills in a sandbox or dry-run mode before approving higher-risk workflows.
- A skill must declare required tools and permissions. It cannot elevate its own privileges.
- Tests must prove that skill execution uses Mission Engine, PolicyGuard, ledger, and verifier rather than bypassing them.

