## 18. Testing and acceptance criteria

Run existing tests first to establish a baseline. Then implement and test changes. Do not report a clean test suite if there were pre-existing failures; distinguish old failures from regressions introduced here.

Acceptance requires:

1. The default Chat screen is materially cleaner: fewer competing cards, less text, clear message/composer hierarchy, and no tall chair stage consuming the page.
2. Morrow remains a recognisable full-body animated companion in a compact Morrow Nook in Chat and a safe floating presence in other views. Click-to-chat and existing animation states work.
3. Morrow's natural idle ladder, focus mode, mission-event expressions and direct sit/run/dance/rest commands continue to work without per-frame model calls.
4. Soul is editable, versioned and persists. Personality template import/export/reset still works, with Morrow as the sole built-in personality.
5. Skills can be created, validated, reused, executed, versioned, tested, disabled and removed; output artifacts and mission/guard/verifier paths are correctly wired.
6. Plugins can be imported, reviewed, sandboxed/isolated where supported, enabled/disabled and removed. Untrusted plugin output cannot bypass rules.
7. AI Browser manual/AI modes, profile selection, safe credential takeover and page-context handoff remain available. Any missing native persistence is clearly reported.
8. IDE file editing, test/lint actions, Git diff, artifact handoff and extension actions accurately reflect what is real versus simulated.
9. Connectors preserve project bindings and scope/write gates. No fake connection states.
10. Scheduler preview, Run Now, execution history, pause/resume and failure policies work through the mission engine.
11. Sleep/Evals and Trust/Ledger views retain their distinctive functionality and are not replaced by decorative dashboard cards.
12. L3xi's corrupted statement tests still detect mismatches; money actions remain draft-only outside the clearly labelled mock bank.
13. Visible buttons and form controls work; long details are collapsed by default but remain accessible.
14. Build/type check/lint and relevant unit/integration/E2E tests run; all outcomes are reported honestly.
15. Every feature is tagged internally in the audit inventory as real, local, simulated, or missing.

